# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AiRA — ignore rules
#
# REWRITTEN for the v1.0 repo. The previous version had three rules that were
# actively dangerous, and they only failed to bite because the affected files
# had been force-added earlier:
#
#   *.json   also matched package.json / package-lock.json / .eslintrc.json.
#            A clean init would have produced a repo that cannot npm install.
#   *.md     sat AFTER the !aira-forecaster-agents/knowledge/… un-ignores, and
#            in gitignore the LAST matching rule wins — so TAX_REFERENCE.md and
#            RMD_TABLES.md, deliberately tracked as the canonical tax constants,
#            were re-ignored.
#   main*    matched anything starting with "main" anywhere in the tree.
#
# Two ordering rules to preserve if you edit this file:
#   1. A later rule overrides an earlier one. Un-ignores (!) must come AFTER
#      the broad rule they carve an exception out of.
#   2. You cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded. To keep
#      one file out of an ignored folder you must ignore `dir/*` (its contents),
#      not `dir` (the directory itself).
#
# And the lesson that made this necessary: .gitignore does nothing for files
# already tracked. Adding a rule here does NOT remove anything from the repo —
# that needs `git rm --cached`. Archive/ was listed here for months while its
# contents sat public.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Dependencies
node_modules

# Build output. Generated from public/ + src/ by `npm run build`; every asset
# in here has a tracked source, so the folder is pure artifact.
/build

# Local tooling / editor / OS
desktop.ini
public/desktop.ini
*-workspace
.vscode

# Secrets and deploy state — never commit
.env
.env.*
.dev.vars
.wrangler
.netlify
/netlify

# ── Personal data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Legacy app builds. These carried a real date of birth, portfolio balance,
# Social Security benefit and domicile, and were public. Never track this again.
Archive/

# Profile data is user-specific by definition — the generic-first rule in
# CLAUDE.md means none of it belongs in the repo.
data/profile.json
profile.json
profile*.json
*.local.json

# Agent memory and definitions — private working notes, synced out-of-band.
memory/
.claude/

# ── Markdown ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only README ships. CLAUDE.md and REQUIREMENTS.md are private planning docs,
# synced between machines outside git.
*.md
!README.md

# ── Agent workspace ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ignore the folder's CONTENTS (not the folder itself, or the un-ignores below
# could not apply), then re-include only the two canonical reference tables.
# These are tracked deliberately: they contain no user data, and keeping them
# untracked meant a correction on one machine never reached the others —
# RMD_TABLES.md carried a wrong age-89 divisor (13.0 vs the IRS 12.9) on two of
# three machines while CLAUDE.md calls these files the canonical source. That
# is a live trap for whoever ports a doc value into code next.
#
# This block is LAST on purpose: its un-ignores must outrank the *.md rule.
aira-forecaster-agents/*
!aira-forecaster-agents/knowledge/
aira-forecaster-agents/knowledge/*
!aira-forecaster-agents/knowledge/TAX_REFERENCE.md
!aira-forecaster-agents/knowledge/RMD_TABLES.md

# ── Local-only tests and reports ─────────────────────────────────────────────
*.local.js
*.local.ts
TEST_REPORT.md
tests/local/
